[0.0, "o", "Investigating REAL data for tenant \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: how much open pipeline do we have right now, broken down by stage and value, and how much of it should i actually believe?\r\n\u001b[2m2026-09-23 12:54:00\u001b[0m [\u001b[33m\u001b[1mwarning  \u001b[0m] \u001b[1mmcp.nothing_admissible        \u001b[0m \u001b[36mlabel\u001b[0m=\u001b[35mposthog\u001b[0m \u001b[36mreason\u001b[0m=\u001b[35m'the server was queried and offered no tool Cortex can admit; every tool must declare readOnlyHint: true'\u001b[0m\r\nRead-only: no write capability exists in the tool registry.\r\nCapabilities available to \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: github, hubspot, posthog, slack\r\n  [  0.1s]          checking what data exists\r\n  [ 12.1s]          found posthog__list_projects\r\n  [ 12.1s]          checking memory for prior context\r\n  [ 21.0s] step 1   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 26.2s] step 1   calling hubspot__pipeline\r\n  [ 26.2s] step 1   calling hubspot__closed_won\r\n  [ 26.2s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 27.9s] step 1   got hubspot__pipeline (2 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 27.9s] step 1   got hubspot__closed_won (3 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 27.9s] step 1   got hubspot__search (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 27.9s] step 2   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 30.7s] step 2   got read hubspot.pipeline in full (73 rows) (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 30.7s] step 3   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 88.8s]          drafting the report from 4 observation(s)\r\n  [128.0s]          checking every citation resolves\r\n  [128.0s]          re-reading each claim against its own evidence\r\n  sufficiency gate: the evidence does NOT support a cause (4.8s); missing: Historical stage-conversion / win-rate data per stage to assess credibility of pipeline amounts; Deal-level activity/engagement logs (last contacted, email opens, meeting history) to judge which open deals are stale or at risk; Source-of-truth criteria for what \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s as 'believable' pipeline (e.g., stalled deals, deals with no recent activity, deals past close_date); Any prior snapshot of pipeline to compare against for a 'movement' or trend\r\n  [145.9s]          writing the report\r\n\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: How much open pipeline do we have right now, broken down by stage and value, and how much of it should I actually believe?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: insufficient evidence\r\nTook 128s over 3 steps, 46,206 tokens, 4 observations gathered, 3 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Open pipeline totals $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 across \u2588\u2588 deals; weighting by HubSpot's own per-deal probability field brings the credible figure down to roughly $\u2588.\u2588M.  [hubspot.pipeline 2a1a5010]\r\n  Roughly $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 of open value sits in a cluster of zero-contact, no-source deals all created on 2026-01-05, a pattern also seen among closed-won records from the same date, suggesting these are legacy/imported records rather than actively worked opportunities and should be dis\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed or verified before being reported as live pipeline.  [hubspot.pipeline 2a1a5010, hubspot.closed_won 74484df5]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Open pipeline totals $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 across \u2588\u2588 deals in \u2588 stages  (medium)\r\n    - Total open pipeline is $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 across \u2588\u2588 open deals.  [hubspot.pipeline 2a1a5010]\r\n    - HubSpot's own probability field ranges from \u2588.\u2588 (stage_\u2588) to \u2588.\u2588 (contractsent), implying a probability-weighted pipeline value well below the raw $\u2588.\u2588\u2588M total \u2014 summing amount*probability across the \u2588\u2588 rows gives roughly $\u2588.\u2588M, though this figure was computed by me from the raw rows rather than returned as a pre-aggregated observation.  [hubspot.pipeline 2a1a5010]\r\n  A large share of 'open' pipeline value sits in stale, contact-less deals from a January bulk import  (medium)\r\n    - These same zero-contact, no-source deals also appear in the closed-won set with identical 2026-01-05 creation timestamps and null source (e.g. \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588), indicating this is a batch of legacy/imported records rather than deals actively worked through a normal source-attributed pipeline.  [hubspot.pipeline 2a1a5010, hubspot.closed_won 74484df5]\r\n  Concentration: two reps and a handful of deals drive most of the value  (medium)\r\n    - A single deal, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 at $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 in presentationscheduled with probability \u2588.\u2588, is the largest open deal and alone represents about \u2588% of total open pipeline value.  [hubspot.pipeline 2a1a5010]\r\n    - Five deals are priced at exactly $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 aside) \u2014 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588, Pax\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588's, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2014 suggesting many of these use a round default/placeholder value rather than a deal-specific estimate.  [hubspot.pipeline 2a1a5010]\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [contradicted] The raw $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 open pipeline figure is a reliable estimate of what will actually close.\r\n      HubSpot's per-deal probability field, ranging \u2588.\u2588-\u2588.\u2588, is populated on every open row and implies expected value well below face value; a probability-weighted figure (~$\u2588.\u2588M) is roughly \u2588\u2588% lower than the raw total. Taking the raw sum at face value over\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s realistic pipeline.\r\n  [inconclusive] The presence of many zero-contact, no-source, same-day-created deals (2026-01-05 batch) indicates a data-quality artifact (bulk import/migration) rather than genuine actively-worked opportunities, and their inclusion inflates the credible open pipeline figure.\r\n      Ten open deals worth ~$\u2588\u2588\u2588k share an identical creation timestamp cluster (2026-01-05), zero associated contacts, and null source/source_detail \u2014 a pattern inconsistent with organically sourced, actively engaged opportunities and consistent with a historical data import. The same signature (same date, zero contacts, null source) appears among closed-won deals too, reinforcing that this is a batch-loaded cohort rather than coincidence.\r\n  [inconclusive] Pipeline value is concentrated among a small number of high-value round-number deals (e.g., multiple identical $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 and $\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 amounts), suggesting some amounts are placeholder estimates rather than deal-specific pricing, which weakens confidence in the precision of the total.\r\n      The clustering of many deals at exactly $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 and $\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 is suggestive of default/round-number entry, but without a CRM field or Slack/deal-note evidence explicitly confirming these are placeholders, this cannot be verified as fact \u2014 it is a pattern worth flagging rather than a confirmed data-quality issue.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P\u2588 Report open pipeline using the probability-weighted figure (~$\u2588.\u2588M) alongside the raw $\u2588.\u2588\u2588M total, rather than the raw total alone.\r\n      why: HubSpot's own per-deal probability field already dis\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s for stage-based close likelihood; using it avoids overstating what is realistically expected to close.\r\n      [hubspot.pipeline 2a1a5010]\r\n  P\u2588 Audit and likely exclude or flag the ~$\u2588\u2588\u2588k cohort of zero-contact, null-source deals created on 2026-01-05 (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) when reporting pipeline to leadership, pending confirmation from \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 on whether these are live opportunities.\r\n      why: These deals share a suspicious batch signature (same creation timestamp, no contacts, no source) matching a pattern also seen among closed-won records from the same date, suggesting a historical import rather than actively engaged pipeline.\r\n      [hubspot.pipeline 2a1a5010, hubspot.closed_won 74484df5]\r\n  P\u2588 Read the full 384a9fa6 observation row-by-row (or confirm it is a duplicate of the pipeline query) before using it as an independent cross-check in future reports.\r\n      why: It was \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed but only its digest was reviewed; while its aggregate figures match the fully-read pipeline observation, per-row content remains unverified.\r\n      [hubspot.search 384a9fa6]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - The full \u2588\u2588-row open-pipeline dataset (evidence 384a9fa6) was \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed but its individual rows were never read in full \u2014 only a digest was reviewed. Any claim requiring specifics from that particular query result beyond what the digest reports has not been verified; the parallel hubspot__pipeline observation (read in full) was used instead for row-level detail, and the two queries returned identical aggregate totals (\u2588\u2588 deals, $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588), giving reasonable confidence they represent the same underlying set.\r\n  - No CRM stage-change history, deal-note, or Slack/GitHub cross-reference was available to independently confirm which deals are being actively worked versus stalled; probability and stage fields are self-reported by reps and may not reflect true likelihood.\r\n  - Close dates for many open deals cluster at period-end boundaries (2026-12-31 appears \u2588\u2588 times, 2026-06-30 \u2588 times), which may reflect sales-ops default date-setting rather than genuine forecasted close timing, further reducing confidence in near-term forecasts derived from this field.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- executive_summary[0]: The $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 total across \u2588\u2588 deals matches payload fields exactly, but the truncated evidence doesn't show the full weighted-sum calculation, so the ~$\u2588.\u2588M figure cannot be verif\r\n- executive_summary[2]: The visible open deals with 2026-01-05 creation, null source, and zero contacts sum to only $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 (BofA $\u2588\u2588\u2588k + \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 $\u2588\u2588\u2588k), not the claimed $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588, though the qualitative\r\n- findings[0].claims[2]: The payload is truncated after ~\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588 rows, so the cited evidence does not actually contain all rows needed to verify the claimed ~$\u2588.\u2588M weighted sum, though the probability fie\r\n- findings[2].claims[2]: All nine named deals (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588, Pax\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588's, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) are indeed listed at exactly $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588, though the claim's \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 of 'five' contra\r\n  - \u2588 causal claim(s) were withheld: a separate check of the evidence gathered, made without seeing this report, found that it does not support a definitive answer about cause. These observations provide raw \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s and dollar totals of open and closed-won deals by stage, which supports a breakdown of pipeline by stage and value, but nothing here establishes causation for any change in pipeline size nor gives a basis for judging reliability/credibility of the open deals beyond their raw stage labels. What would settle it: Historical stage-conversion / win-rate data per stage to assess credibility of pipeline amounts; Deal-level activity/engagement logs (last contacted, email opens, meeting history) to judge which open deals are stale or at risk; Source-of-truth criteria for what \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s as 'believable' pipeline (e.g., stalled deals, deals with no recent activity, deals past close_date); Any prior snapshot of pipeline to compare against for a 'movement' or trend. What remains describes what h\r\n  - The question also asked about What is the actual breakdown of pipeline value by each of the \u2588 stages (amounts per stage)? \u2014 this report does not address that. What it does say is grounded; it is not the whole answer.\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - hubspot.search (384a9fa6) was retrieved as a cross-check on open deals but only its digest was reviewed, not its \u2588\u2588 individual rows; conclusions rely on the separately fully-read hubspot.pipeline observation instead.\r\n  - Deal probability, stage, and close_date fields are self-reported CRM inputs by sales reps and were not cross-validated against any external activity log (e.g., email/call engagement, contract systems).\r\n  - The github commits sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github deployments sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github issues sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github links sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog annotations sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog events sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  74484df5  hubspot.closed_won  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closed_won=2026-01-01..2026-09-23\r\n  2a1a5010  hubspot.pipeline  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?open=true\r\n  384a9fa6  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?hs_is_closed=false\r\n\r\nphase breakdown (146s wall, 143s measured)\r\n  phase        calls  seconds  share    mean  tokens\r\n  survey           1     12.0    8%    12.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  recall           1      8.9    6%     8.9  in 0 out 0\r\n  loop_model       3     66.1   45%    22.0  in 6 out 7,615 cached 20,827\r\n  loop_tools       2      1.7    1%     0.8  in 0 out 0\r\n  draft            1     39.1   27%    39.1  in 34,641 out 3,944\r\n  gate             1      0.0    0%     0.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  verify           1     10.3    7%    10.3  in 46,739 out 1,681\r\n  sufficiency      1      4.8    3%     4.8  in 4,041 out 282\r\n  unmeasured              2.9    2%\r\n  cache hit rate: 20%\r\n"]
